    {
      "source": "src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/postconciliar/roman-missal-third-edition-en-us-2011/propers/temporal/pc-s55-twenty-ninth-sunday-in-ordinary-time-year-a/sections/20-texts.tex",
      "paragraph": 4,
      "matches": false,
      "text": "Isaiah 45:1,4--6; U.S. Lectionary no.145. Verses 2--3 are not in this appointment.\n1 Thus saith the Lord to my anointed Cyrus, whose right hand I have taken hold of, to subdue nations before his face, and to turn the backs of kings, and to open the doors before him, and the gates shall not be shut."
    },
    {
      "source": "src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/postconciliar/roman-missal-third-edition-en-us-2011/propers/temporal/pc-s55-twenty-ninth-sunday-in-ordinary-time-year-a/sections/20-texts.tex",
      "paragraph": 8,
      "matches": false,
      "text": "Psalm 96:1,3,4--5,7--8,9--10a,c (Hebrew; Vulgate/Douay 95), response 7b; Lectionary no.145. The response uses part of verse 7, not the whole verse. The following study text gives complete verses 7 and 10: verse 10's middle clause about the world's stability is context only and is not appointed. It is retained here visibly as part of a complete Bible verse, not restored to the sung strophe.\n1 A canticle for David himself, when the house was built after the captivity. Sing ye to the Lord a new canticle: sing to the Lord, all the earth."
    },
    {
      "source": "src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/postconciliar/roman-missal-third-edition-en-us-2011/propers/temporal/pc-s55-twenty-ninth-sunday-in-ordinary-time-year-a/sections/20-texts.tex",
      "paragraph": 16,
      "matches": false,
      "text": "1 Thessalonians 1:1--5b; Lectionary no.145. The reading ends before verse 5's final clause about the missionaries' conduct. The complete verse 5 below includes that final clause as unappointed context.\n1 Paul and Sylvanus and Timothy to the church of the Thessalonians: in God the Father and in the Lord Jesus Christ."
    },
    {
      "source": "src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/postconciliar/roman-missal-third-edition-en-us-2011/propers/temporal/pc-s55-twenty-ninth-sunday-in-ordinary-time-year-a/sections/20-texts.tex",
      "paragraph": 21,
      "matches": false,
      "text": "Philippians 2:15d,16a; Lectionary no.145. Only the short portions concerning shining in the world and holding the word of life are appointed. The rest of these complete verses is context, not additional acclamation text.\n15 That you may be blameless and sincere children of God, without reproof, in the midst of a crooked and perverse generation: among whom you shine as lights in the world."
    },
    {
      "source": "src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/postconciliar/roman-missal-third-edition-en-us-2011/propers/temporal/pc-s55-twenty-ninth-sunday-in-ordinary-time-year-a/sections/20-texts.tex",
      "paragraph": 23,
      "matches": false,
      "text": "Matthew 22:15--21; Lectionary no.145. No shorter form is appointed for this Year A Gospel.\n15 Then the Pharisees going, consulted among themselves how to insnare him in his speech."
    },
    {
      "source": "src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/postconciliar/roman-missal-third-edition-en-us-2011/propers/temporal/pc-s55-twenty-ninth-sunday-in-ordinary-time-year-a/sections/60-history.tex",
      "paragraph": 2,
      "matches": false,
      "text": "Entrance: cf. Psalm 16:6,8 (Vulgate; Hebrew 17).\n\\chronodate{entrance}{\\chronologyannotation{entrance}}"
    },
    {
      "source": "src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/postconciliar/roman-missal-third-edition-en-us-2011/propers/temporal/pc-s55-twenty-ninth-sunday-in-ordinary-time-year-a/sections/60-history.tex",
      "paragraph": 4,
      "matches": false,
      "text": "Communion option: cf. Psalm 32:18--19 (Vulgate; Hebrew 33).\n\\chronodate{communion-psalm}{\\chronologyannotation{communion-psalm}}"
    },
    {
      "source": "src/gpt/liturgy/roman-rite/postconciliar/roman-missal-third-edition-en-us-2011/propers/temporal/pc-s55-twenty-ninth-sunday-in-ordinary-time-year-a/sections/60-history.tex",
